14
00:00:35.885 --> 00:00:39.618
This chapter covers two connected population-scale systems.

15
00:00:39.898 --> 00:00:40.538
1.

16
00:00:40.818 --> 00:01:03.922
A national digital identity platform, in the style of India's Aadhaar: enrolment of more than a billion residents, with demographic and biometric capture;. biometric de-duplication, so each person gets exactly one ID;. online authentication (fingerprint, iris, face, OTP) at hundreds of millions of requests a day;. eKYC with consent;.

17
00:01:05.272 --> 00:01:12.205
virtual IDs and tokenisation for privacy;. the ecosystem of registered agencies and devices.

18
00:01:12.485 --> 00:01:13.189
2.

19
00:01:13.469 --> 00:01:35.528
A vaccination-scale registration and certificate platform, in the style of CoWIN: registering hundreds of millions of people in weeks;. booking slots at centres, with flash crowds when new age groups open;. recording each dose at the centre, sometimes offline;. issuing digitally signed QR certificates that anyone can verify offline;.

20
00:01:36.878 --> 00:01:38.947
dashboards for supply and coverage.

21
00:01:39.227 --> 00:01:56.166
Also covered: the algorithms (biometric matching and de-duplication at scale, liveness detection, identity token design, slot allocation under scarcity, bot defence, signature schemes for verifiable credentials), the data platform and the tech stack.

